1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,417
After 14 months, my secured
card got upgraded to a real
unsecured card and I got my
$300 deposit back.

2
00:00:07,417 --> 00:00:20,769
I was 24 with a 581 credit
score and basically no
credit history. I had one
medical collection from two
years earlier and zero open
accounts. I figured a
secured card was my only
real option.

3
00:00:20,769 --> 00:00:42,281
I opened the secured card,
put down my $300 deposit,
and then barely used it.
Like maybe $8 a month
because I thought keeping
the balance low meant
keeping it near zero. My
utilization was fine but my
payment history was thin,
and I let 8 months go by
without asking for a review
or doing anything proactive.

4
00:00:42,281 --> 00:01:08,614
I started charging exactly
$60 to $90 a month, which
kept me under 30%
utilization on the $300
limit. I set up autopay for
the full statement balance
so I never missed a payment.
At the 12-month mark I
called the issuer directly
and asked about their
graduation criteria. They
told me 12 on-time payments
qualified me for a review.
Two months later, they
upgraded my account and
refunded my deposit.

5
00:01:08,614 --> 00:01:15,661
A secured card only works if
you treat it like a tool,
not a backup card you forget
about.

6
00:01:15,661 --> 00:01:20,483
Follow for more real credit
stories, or drop a question
in the comments.
